    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/23 P.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Pyatifanov put you up to this, didn’t he? It’s all just a game to him."


translate english d4_police_forced_44d93692:


    "Romka rolled his eyes."


translate english d4_police_forced_0b3c9119:



    voice "voice/romka/4day/151Z.ogg"
    Rom "Not this shit again..."


translate english d4_police_forced_ad06657e:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/79. Nek.ogg"
    Ant "Nobody put me up to this!"


translate english d4_police_forced_0653b30f:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/80. Yasam.ogg"
    Ant "I wanted to find the killer myself."


translate english d4_police_forced_ef71a20f:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/24 Eto.ogg"
    Tikhonov "You got lucky you stumbled upon me."


translate english d4_police_forced_9e337fbf:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/25 A.ogg"
    Tikhonov "And after I asked you nicely to stay home!"


translate english d4_police_forced_e9f1e971:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/26 Na.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Why the hell do you even need that killer for?"


translate english d4_police_forced_921f3934:


    "I lowered my head in embarrassment."


translate english d4_police_forced_e5a00238:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/80. Nag.ogg"
    Ant "I want the reward."


translate english d4_police_forced_07338303:


    "Senior lieutenant crossed his hands on his chest and heaved a deep sigh."


translate english d4_police_forced_0ebfe7e2:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/28 De.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Money, huh? And why do you need so much money?"


translate english d4_police_forced_67c1cd43:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/81. U.ogg"
    Ant "My parents are in debt..."


translate english d4_police_forced_0e9c22d8:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/29 Da.ogg"
    Tikhonov "The whole country is balls deep in debt! So what?"


translate english d4_police_forced_31c1e23f:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/30 Du.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Do you think it would help if you went missing, too?"


translate english d4_police_forced_abe8bdc3:


    "I sniffed, upset."


translate english d4_police_forced_6ac6d3b0:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/01 Da.ogg"
    Ant "Nothing can help them by now! They can’t live a single day without fighting!"


translate english d4_police_forced_af70f278:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/02 Pro.ogg"
    Ant "I just want Olya and I to be happy."


translate english d4_police_forced_ef41af14:


    "Tikhonov thought for a bit, drumming his fingers against the table that had a stack of papers on top."


translate english d4_police_forced_d9b122ef:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/31 Ne.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Don’t cry, boy. It’ll be alright."


translate english d4_police_forced_e2ac7cb2:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/32 E.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Your parents will make up, and we’ll find that killer..."


translate english d4_police_forced_7ecefe32:



    voice "voice/romka/4day/152 A.ogg"
    Rom "Yeah, and the country will prosper."


translate english d4_police_forced_1c74d7a7:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/33 P.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Watch your tongue, Pyatifanov!"


translate english d4_police_forced_4c4b0bac:


    "Tikhonov flashed us his sturdy teeth, but I still decided to stand my ground. For my Olya's sake."


translate english d4_police_forced_e2bf1d34:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/34 A.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Ah, to hell with it!"


translate english d4_police_forced_e14ad4bc:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/35 W.ogg"
    Tikhonov "I’ll just reprimand you this time."


translate english d4_police_forced_8bd7c624:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/36 No.ogg"
    Tikhonov "But I won’t be this lenient again."


translate english d4_police_forced_69a35833:


    "He waved his finger at us."


translate english d4_police_forced_549fac86:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/37U .ogg"
    Tikhonov "If I ever see you skulk in the darkness again, I’ll give you what for!"


translate english d4_police_common_a5cf9b6e:


    "Bulanova let out her last whimper. The room descended into complete silence."


translate english d4_police_common_d3bb54f7:


    "As if on autopilot, I wandered toward the notice board, leaving wet footprints in my wake."


translate english d4_police_common_b283b919:


    "I just stood in front of it, staring at the photos of Senechka, Semyon, and Katya. They stared back at me."


translate english d4_police_common_1f22e458:


    "When Tikhonov’s hand landed on my shoulder, I couldn’t help but shudder."


translate english d4_police_common_375d5998:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/38 Eh.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Oh, Anton. If only you knew how often I look at them."


translate english d4_police_common_2e594aa6:



    voice "voice/romka/4day/153 L.ogg"
    Rom "Shouldn't you be catching the criminal, not staring at pictures?"


translate english d4_police_common_9f5c5118:


    "I thought that Tikhonov would get mad, but he swallowed Romka’s brazen remark."


translate english d4_police_common_9146a48a:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/39 Po.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Do you think I don’t want to lock the bracelets around that bastard’s wrists?"


translate english d4_police_common_dd002174:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/40 Vz.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Or grab him by his hands and put him against the wall?"


translate english d4_police_common_f82113f4:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/41 Da.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Every day, I wake up and go to bed with those thoughts!"


translate english d4_police_common_820cdd1e:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/42 Zn.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Do you have any idea what I see in my dreams? You’re better off not knowing."


translate english d4_police_common_2caea3d6:


    "He slouched as if his thoughts were that heavy, and then walked slowly toward his desk, sighing."


translate english d4_police_common_7aa742b4:


    "We listened to him in silence."


translate english d4_police_common_8f513653:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/43 De.ogg"
    Tikhonov "This is a cold case!"


translate english d4_police_common_c371a61c:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/44 Na.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Yes, we found some child footprints that led into the forest, about one hundred fifty feet into it. But then they just disappear."


translate english d4_police_common_9048ca91:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/45 A.ogg"
    Tikhonov "And it only gets weirder from that..."


translate english d4_police_common_182ac67d:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/46 Pr.ogg"
    Tikhonov "We asked for a canine unit. But the dogs wouldn’t catch the trail, they just kept on whimpering."


translate english d4_police_common_c3f3c8b0:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/47 S.ogg"
    Tikhonov "We scoured the forest with a group of volunteers and found not a single clue."


translate english d4_police_common_9c35e3eb:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/48 D.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Six acres of land, stomped with our boots... Is that killer hiding in animal holes or something?"


translate english d4_police_common_1fc48dcf:


    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/49 A.ogg"


translate english d4_police_common_ac354877:


    Tikhonov "And then one of the locals claimed that he heard children laughing at night."


translate english d4_police_common_a889a6d2:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/50 M.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Said that the missing kids came to him from the afterlife and looked into his window."


translate english d4_police_common_4eb59dd3:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/51 S.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Everyone’s going insane!"


translate english d4_police_common_5c8be5e3:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/52 Es.ogg"
    Tikhonov "And then the evidence started disappearing..."


translate english d4_police_common_ac4e5268:


    "The lieutenant massaged his nose bridge."


translate english d4_police_common_13eb84bf:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/53 A.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Come to think of it, something like this had already happened in our village..."


translate english d4_police_common_2ba69f66:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/54 Po.ogg"
    Tikhonov "There was a similar case here thirty years ago. The kids went missing, just like this time."


translate english d4_police_common_90ba472b:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/55 Ho.ogg"
    Tikhonov "And even though they never found the kidnapper, the police did a better job that time. They saved two of the kids."


translate english d4_police_common_035d96be:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/56 V.ogg"
    Tikhonov "I’ve been keeping this as a memento since that day."


translate english d4_police_common_38166c2d:


    "The policeman carefully handed me a poster, yellowed from time."


translate english d4_police_common_76792f09:



    voice "voice/romka/4day/154 V.ogg"
    Rom "Seriously?"


translate english d4_police_common_fcf1e790:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/03 Ta.ogg"
    Ant "So it was you?"


translate english d4_police_common_54a1adff:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/57 T.ogg"
    Tikhonov "That’s right."


translate english d4_police_common_b6781ac8:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/58 ya.ogg"
    Tikhonov "I visited this station for the first time when I was around your age."


translate english d4_police_common_5c233b09:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/59 P.ogg"
    Tikhonov "It was a windy, snowy winter day..."


translate english d4_police_common_94f17027:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/61 No.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Yet, even now, I just can’t remember what happened to me."


translate english d4_police_common_b588a649:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/61 Na.ogg"
    Tikhonov "The precinct officer at the time found me in the taiga."


translate english d4_police_common_2294191b:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/62 Go.ogg"
    Tikhonov "He said he found me unconscious, covered in pine needles..."


translate english d4_police_common_c0849e50:


    "Tikhonov tilted his head, drowning in the fog of his fragmented memories."


translate english d4_police_common_bd981646:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/63 Eto.ogg"
    Tikhonov "It’s thanks to him that I’m not abandoning this hopeless case."


translate english d4_police_common_a90033ad:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/64 Do.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Getting to the bottom of this is my duty."


translate english d4_police_common_d026205a:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/04 Viska.ogg"
    Ant "You said they saved two children. Who was the second one?"


translate english d4_police_common_fdbf4fb1:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/65 da.ogg"
    Tikhonov "You won’t believe it if I tell you! The second kid was a girl..."


translate english d4_police_common_b71a0d28:


    "Tikhonov wasn’t able to finish the sentence."


translate english d4_police_common_a1ed1153:


    "The door flew open and, along with the blowing wind, Lilia Pavlovna staggered into the station, gasping for air."


translate english d4_police_common_c404f2ca:


    "I jumped up from surprise and stood at attention, but the teacher didn’t even notice us."


translate english d4_police_common_6304cb12:



    voice "voice/lydia/4day/22 Net.ogg"
    Teacher "She’s gone! She hasn’t returned home!"


translate english d4_police_common_0b120a0a:



    voice "voice/lydia/4day/23 Vi.ogg"
    Teacher "You said that she will, that she may be at a friend’s house, but she hasn’t returned!"


translate english d4_police_common_77424340:



    voice "voice/lydia/4day/24 Net.ogg"
    Teacher "My Katya is gone..."


translate english d4_police_common_c6c5a0d1:


    "Lilia Pavlovna wailed while covering her face with her hands. Romka and I exchanged quick glances."


translate english d4_police_common_4d58211b:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/66 Us.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Calm down! Stop screaming!"


translate english d4_police_common_fa7b684c:



    voice "voice/lydia/4day/26 Da.ogg"
    Teacher "How can I calm down?! My dear Katya..."


translate english d4_police_common_1eae7781:


    "The lieutenant hugged Lilia Pavlovna by the shoulders and gave a curt nod our way."


translate english d4_police_common_d7dc1155:



    voice "voice/tihonov/4day/67 Br.ogg"
    Tikhonov "Scram!"


translate english d4_police_common_6fc5d692:


    "We backed out into the doorway, toward the wind's merciless whipping."


translate english d4_police_common_51645a36:



    voice "voice/romka/4day/155 D.ogg"
    Rom "Tough luck! The cops are useless."


translate english d4_police_common_ba1d3ffb:



    voice "voice/romka/4day/156 O.ogg"
    Rom "We can only rely on ourselves."


translate english d4_police_common_b8dff539:


    "At that moment, I felt like there was nothing else in the world apart from the wind and the long shadows that wandered in the dark."


translate english d4_police_common_c1be798f:


    "And that we were also destined to become such shadows."


translate english d4_police_common_31db550c:


    "Romka stretched out his hand to say goodbye."


translate english d4_police_common_b2a24a4e:


    "I felt like the moment I loosen my grip on his palm, I’ll wake up in the forest without my memories. Unless I get eaten alive, of course."


translate english d4_police_common_f8a0086c:


    "He let go of my hand and left."


translate english d4_police_common_52aef795:


    "I squirmed in the freezing cold, hesitant to leave the illuminated circle in front of the police station."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_59a11abf:


    "The village looked abandoned, desolate."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_112cabb8:


    "Rickety fences, ravines full of garbage..."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_bf3619cc:


    "This place probably looks nice in the summer since it's full of greenery. But during winter, under the icy crust, under the snowy blanket..."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_1285d3e6:


    "I turned around from time to time to check if my good friends, who weren't good or friendly to me anymore, were following in my wake."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_20ba5488:


    "Dogs barked and clanged their chains behind the fences, but they grew quiet the moment we reached the next house."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_043d5998:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/22 Pre.ogg"
    Ant "Try imagining that ghosts are clanging with those chains."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_49828320:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/50 O.ogg"
    Pol "Oh, I love ghost stories. Grandpa tells them all the time..."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_2bd93050:


    "She stopped in front of a small but cozy-looking house with a snow-covered roof. Then put her hand on the small gate."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_7fe4117d:


    "Her eyes piercing me as if trying to peek into the depths of my soul."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_c6512ea8:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/51 Vo.ogg"
    Pol "You see, I always mention how good, caring, and smart my grandpa is, but it's only half of the truth."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_d929e187:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/52 V.ogg"
    Pol "Lately, he's been acting sort of..."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_2963308f:


    "She paused, searching for the right words."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_33730028:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/53 Chu.ogg"
    Pol "Funny? Yeah, that's it."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_85904592:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/54 Sta.ogg"
    Pol "He became like that as he aged. So, please, try not to be surprised by him."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_ab72117d:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/23 Tak.ogg"
    Ant "Sir, yes sir! No acting surprised!"


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_1ea66c22:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/55 Ha.ogg"
    Pol "Ahaha! At ease, soldier!"


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_6dfaef92:


    "We walked toward the house on a thin cleaned path."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_5ecec09e:


    "Polina unlocked the door."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_ffa859e8:


    "The long hallway was full of shadows."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_2c8a665d:


    "The door slammed shut behind our backs, cutting us off from the roaring wind and all other outside sounds."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_7cf1775d:


    "The place became so silent that I could hear Polina's heart beating."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_73f10f75:


    "I wanted to cover it with my hand and feel it with my palm, with my {u}life lines.{/u}"


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_44bbce30:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/56 Ti.ogg"
    Pol "Do you always freeze like this?"


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_2a197947:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/57 Ka.ogg"
    Pol "As if somebody pulled an emergency break in your head."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_4993fef0:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/24 Fa.ogg"
    Ant "My imagination is running wild."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_a3d9ba25:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/58 A.ogg"
    Pol "Ah, I see."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_58cfc42d:


    "She took off her coat and hanged it on a wall hook."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_d62cdfbe:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/59 Ra.ogg"
    Pol "Come on, take your stuff off."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_5d021f91:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/60 Ya.ogg"
    Pol "I'll go clean up the room in the meantime."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_ffd164a0:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/61 De.ogg"
    Pol "Grandpa always forgets his things everywhere."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_ae0fc743:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/62 Ya.ogg"
    Pol "I'll be quick."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_a3535563:


    "She floated away, light as a butterfly."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_ffa169e9:


    "Another butterfly, of a steel kind, had a real chance of floating inside my gut in the near future."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_2a813ff1:


    "I took off my coat. Untied my shoelaces."


translate english d4_polhouse_begin_devend_01ffdaa9:


    "A tiny squeak reached my ears."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_ski_d5ceb66d:


    "Just a pair of skis."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_ski_d2c0e28b:


    "A pair of \"Tourist\" skis. Dad told me stories of how he would make his own skis and ski poles, and even his own ski wax from beeswax, rosin, and pine resin."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_ski_5b4160a3:


    "A good fit for the harsh winters around here. But these skis are in need of maintenance. The bindings are in very bad condition. And they have dark red spots on them. Probably just rust."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_telephone_bed2597b:


    "Just a regular phone."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_telephone_e02e5252:


    "If one were to stand in front of the phone, the wallpaper patterns would look like a set of watchful eyes. So this is the place Polina called me from!"


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_telephone_c37e9cf7:


    "She stood right here, under the electric meter, among the shadows, twirling the phone cord. Maybe she even played with the light switch, turning the lights off at times and speaking to me in the dark."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_horns_eb268588:


    "Antlers. Just a wall decoration."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_horns_a376514e:


    "I don't get why adults hang something like this in their homes. Crooked, sharp outgrowths. I've read that animals don't get hurt when their horns that had already hardened get trimmed."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_horns_683f3c5c:


    "Still, it's the same as plastering your wall with clipped fingernails. They are also cornified objects that were once part of a living organism."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_portrait_74ed862e:


    "Paganini's portrait. Spooky."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_portrait_6e3f5c00:


    "I know this painting. Paganini. The guy was so good at playing the violin that other people had decided he sold his soul to the devil."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_portrait_73681238:


    "This portrait was drawn by Nicolai Fechin. He was a famous Russian painter that moved to America after the revolution and became famous there, too. Wow, Paganini has such long fingers."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_portrait_41e81c92:


    "And such a piercing stare. What is he looking at? Maybe he did sell his soul, after all? Would Polina sell hers, I wonder?"


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_66c831ab:


    "What a weird mirror."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_9b6bcc6e:


    "The reflections in this mirror are so sharp and deep... My gaze drowns in it."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_38e46394:


    "It feels more like a doorway than a mirror, with an identical room with skis and sticky-to-the-touch wallpaper behind it."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_1b9daf17:


    "And the electric meter, which barely worked during the last month as if Polina and her grandpa spend their evening in complete darkness."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_1880689e:


    "And then..."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_d4598a38:


    "Huh?! Is there someone there or is it just a factory defect twisting the doors inside the mirror?{w=.7}{nw}"


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_mirror_49362450:


    "Phew... Just a hunting trophy."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_grandfather_f4582e81:


    "That's the room of Polina's grandpa."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_grandfather_d3a70eda:


    "Wow, there's so much junk here, just like in a junk shop!"


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_grandfather_819ae9a2:


    "Or like at the village cemetery dump, where people throw away plastic flowers, splinters from rotten crosses, and dirty stripes with gilded words of condolences."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_grandfather_7c2b6348:


    "Why did I think Polina's grandpa brought all of this from a cemetery dump? Those don't have toys… or a tambourine like in those books about Northern shamans."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_grandfather_169bad4b:


    "And this… what was it called again? A dreamcatcher, I think. It didn't catch any dreams, but it did catch a haymaker spider."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround_grandfather_03076bce:


    "And the stench… No wonder I can hear flies buzzing in this place even in the middle of winter. It smells like thawed lard and wet soil. I guess you just get used to it if you stay here long enough."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_4cfc1bc1:


    "I looked into the deeper part of the house while taking off my boots."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_64b5dc8d:


    "Semi-dark masked the corner at the end of the corridor. Something moved toward me, making the dry floorboards squeak."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_65a93fcf:


    "Squeak, squeak!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_65a93fcf_1:


    "Squeak, squeak!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_0d42b28c:


    "The sound grew louder."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_cf4f436d:


    "I realized that I stepped back toward the door without thinking."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_b6cbe8db:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/25 Pol.ogg"
    Ant "Polina?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_0b73b2db:


    "A wheelchair appeared from around the corner. A stocky old man protruded from the darkness."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d407c379:



    voice "voice/Hariton/01. Ti.ogg"
    Ded "You must be my Polya's classmate, right?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_0363cdc6:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/26 Da.ogg"
    Ant "Yes. My name's Anton Petrov."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_53463894:


    "We shook hands. His grip was surprisingly firm."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_8cf9fef1:



    voice "voice/Hariton/02. Ochen.ogg"
    Ded "Good to meet you! Very good."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_a1baa347:



    voice "voice/Hariton/03. A.ogg"
    Ded "And I'm Khariton. A name of Greek origin, it means 'charitable'."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d06ca50f:



    voice "voice/Hariton/04.At.ogg"
    Ded "And do you know the meaning of your name?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_bbdc758d:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/27 Ni.ogg"
    Ant "I've never thought about it."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d3f2eaf8:



    voice "voice/Hariton/05. Ot.ogg"
    Ded "It comes from Latin 'anteo', someone who goes into battle!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_a3d31647:


    "I chuckled in reply."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_c3884267:


    "Apparently, my name has \"brave\" roots."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9ec95159:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/28 APo.ogg"
    Ant "And Polina?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_57901091:



    voice "voice/Hariton/05.pol.ogg"
    Ded "Polina is a name of French origin."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d1134cb1:



    voice "voice/Hariton/06.Esli.ogg" 
    Ded "If I remember correctly... it means 'sunlight'."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_4ee1022e:


    "Of course. The sunlight, the enchanting views of France, the Parisian sky... all of that sounded like Polina."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_6764cffe:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/29 Vi.ogg"
    Ant "You know a lot about names."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_42ad5d53:



    voice "voice/Hariton/06.Ya.ogg"
    Ded "I gave all my dolls unique names."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_405aeaaa:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/113. Kuk.ogg"
    Ant "Dolls?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_64425a5c:



    voice "voice/Hariton/07. Pol.ogg"
    Ded "Haven't Polina told you? I used to work as a puppeteer in a theater."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_44a0ec25:



    voice "voice/Hariton/08.Pot.ogg"
    Ded "Then, one day, a night guard fell asleep while smoking there. He died and the theater burned down."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_fe142b5d:



    voice "voice/Hariton/09.Ku.ogg"
    Ded "All my dolls burned down."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ebe32bf1:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/114. Za.ogg"
    Ant "What a shame."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ba8ac7da:


    "I was pretty sure that Polina told me her grandpa was a local historian..."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d8f1796c:


    "He squinted."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_5bea44ea:



    voice "voice/Hariton/07. Az.ogg"
    Ded "And have you heard, Anton Petrov, that people in the ages past used to have two names? Their true name, and the one they shared with strangers?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_1e3addd5:



    voice "voice/Hariton/08.Sh.ogg"
    Ded "It was believed that if a person's true name ended up in the hands of bad people, it could spell disaster for its owner."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_25146d83:



    voice "voice/Hariton/09.Po.ogg"
    Ded "Those names could be used to hex or even kill."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_70750c1d:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/115. Ogo.ogg"
    Ant "Really?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_b2dc1da9:



    voice "voice/Hariton/10.V.ogg"
    Ded "Yes, really!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9b01818c:



    voice "voice/Hariton/11.Iz.ogg"
    Ded "And the names they gave to animals were also deliberate."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_72787d6c:



    voice "voice/Hariton/12.Za.ogg"
    Ded "{u}Zayats{/u} comes from 'zaisti' in Lithuanian, 'a hopper'. And {u}volk{/u} comes from Old Slavonic 'vlek', 'one who drags'."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_c984bc91:


    "Khariton drove closer and crossed his hands on his chest."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_2903122d:


    "I wondered to myself where Polina's parents were."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_fb93035f:


    "She never spoke about her mom, only about her grandpa."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_b3370c24:


    "I decided to ask a question to continue the conversation."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_7bd08223:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/116. A.ogg"
    Ant "And what about the bear?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_7ccbb995:



    voice "voice/Hariton/13.O.ogg"
    Ded "Oh! The bear's name is still a mystery."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_6f856b86:



    voice "voice/Hariton/14.N.ogg"
    Ded "Our ancestors were so afraid of that beast, they decided to forget the word they used to call it with."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_94fff887:



    voice "voice/Hariton/15.Ono.ogg"
    Ded "It just disappeared from their language."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_84f97a41:



    voice "voice/Hariton/16. Vm.ogg"
    Ded "We were left with a much more recent interpretation: {u}'one who oversees the honey'{/u}."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_7283cb16:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/117. En.ogg"
    Ant "Sounds interesting."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_a5ae4253:


    "The old man's smile became wider, revealing a stockade of metal implants."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9dc48422:


    "He raised his hand and waved it in the air like a rake that was scratching at empty space."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_039a6521:



    voice "voice/Hariton/18.Sk.ogg"
    Ded "Scratch, scratch, scratch..."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d1a60132:


    "The squeaking sound made me shrink instinctively."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9b95bd0d:



    voice "voice/Hariton/19.To.ogg"
    Ded "{u}Here comes the bear,{/u} оn a fake hind leg, with a long birch cane."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ccd0329b:



    voice "voice/Hariton/19.Vse.ogg"
    Ded "The whole village sleeps, all the peasants sleep."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_da3e6bc8:



    voice "voice/Hariton/19.Odn.ogg"
    Ded "One old hag is awake, sitting on my skin."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_0dee785b:



    voice "voice/Hariton/19.Mo.ogg"
    Ded "Spinning my brown fur, feasting on my flesh."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_20bb698d:


    "If this was what Polina warned me about, I had already broken my promise."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_a47d498c:


    "It's not like I got surprised, more like I became seriously concerned."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_413883f3:



    voice "voice/Hariton/20.Po.ogg"
    Ded "According to legends, that morbid tale happened right in our village... just like many others."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ca715848:



    voice "voice/Hariton/21Vot.ogg"
    Ded "There's also this one..."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_57b736ee:



    voice "voice/Hariton/21.Vpro.ogg"
    Ded "The previous century was tough on simple folk."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_c2633147:



    voice "voice/Hariton/21.Den.ogg"
    Ded "They had close to no money, and even less food. Just like nowadays."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_80f649eb:



    voice "voice/Hariton/22. Po.ogg"
    Ded "Peasants resorted to robbing... of the Taiga, that is. A crucian here, a goose there."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_fc313381:



    voice "voice/Hariton/23.A.ogg"
    Ded "And the chief gamekeeper... Not only didn't he prevent them from doing so, but he also spearheaded the poaching efforts."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_df0a931b:



    voice "voice/Hariton/24.S.ogg"
    Ded "He became the richest man in the village. His cellar was almost ready to burst."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_0e2271e4:



    voice "voice/Hariton/25.Tak.ogg"
    Ded "The gamekeeper boasted everywhere he went: 'This forest is mine! I'm the master here!'"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ec371c7c:



    voice "voice/Hariton/26.Ob.ogg"
    Ded "Then he formed a family, got himself a bunch of servants, and a humble estate."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_f6322e9f:



    voice "voice/Hariton/27.E.ogg"
    Ded "It was such a joyful occasion that he ordered a feast that spanned for the whole day, up until the night. When the clock struck twelve, though, dogs started barking outside."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9f8c341c:



    voice "voice/Hariton/29. Ed.ogg"
    Ded "'Go,' the gamemaster shouted to his servants, 'throw some bones to the dogs.'"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_aa83d441:



    voice "voice/Hariton/30.Ch.ogg"
    Ded "Time passed, and somebody knocked on his gates."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_c7117d16:



    voice "voice/Hariton/31. Ede.ogg"
    Ded "'Go,' he shouted to his family, 'chase away the guests.'"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_616375d4:



    voice "voice/Hariton/32.O.ogg"
    Ded "He was left alone at the table. Not a single soul was coming back."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_7f8afd2a:



    voice "voice/Hariton/33.Sl.ogg"
    Ded "The he heard dogs howling, only to go silent again."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_fc0715cd:



    voice "voice/Hariton/34.E.ogg"
    Ded "And then! Someone started banging on his door!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_2103ed31:



    voice "voice/Hariton/34.B.ogg"
    Ded "Bam, bam, bam!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_e668ed8f:


    "I licked my parched lips and instinctively looked over the old man's shoulder, praying in my mind that Polina would come back soon and interrupt this eerie monologue."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_78b837d8:


    "Yet only shadows writhed behind Khariton's back."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_2b4fc4e9:



    voice "voice/Hariton/35.E.ogg"
    Ded "The gamemaster got scared to death and ran to the cellar."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_60a7e4ba:



    voice "voice/Hariton/35.Z.ogg"
    Ded "He slammed the lock shut. Then, suddenly, somebody spoke from the outside."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_c1663a9b:



    voice "voice/Hariton/36. M.ogg"
    Ded "Love, it's me, your wife. Open up."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_d50c0488:



    voice "voice/Hariton/37.V.ogg"
    Ded "No way, never."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_a56b6c35:



    voice "voice/Hariton/38. G.ogg"
    Ded "The voice became harsher, more forceful."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_14e2a997:



    voice "voice/Hariton/39. Ez.ogg"
    Ded "I'm starving, love, at least give me something from our supplies."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_efeb413b:



    voice "voice/Hariton/40.U.ogg"
    Ded "'Begone! In the name of the Lord!' the gamemaster shouted and fell to his knees in prayer."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_e66e5784:



    voice "voice/Hariton/41.T.ogg"
    Ded "The next moment, the voice roared."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_6b5b6034:



    voice "voice/Hariton/42.C.ogg"
    Ded "If you won't come out in one piece, at least give me a slice!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_555a5356:



    voice "voice/Hariton/43.Eg.ogg"
    Ded "The game master spent the rest of the night inside, trembling from fear."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9b40d682:



    voice "voice/Hariton/44. A.ogg"
    Ded "And when he gathered enough bravery to come out, he found his family and servants..."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9cc6d6f2:



    voice "voice/Hariton/45.P.ogg"
    Ded "...hanged on their own guts along the main road."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_bd65d54f:



    voice "voice/Hariton/46. G.ogg"
    Ded "In the blink of an eye, his manor became infested with wild beasts."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_41badca5:



    voice "voice/Hariton/47.P.ogg"
    Ded "Because the Taiga has no bounds, one part of it exists in our world, and the other—in a place where night never ends."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_39bc5074:



    voice "voice/Hariton/49. E.ogg"
    Ded "The gamemaster tried to escape the accursed village, but the true Forest Master got to him in the end."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ed49474d:


    "I spoke in a shaky voice."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_f1c00476:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/118. E.ogg"
    Ant "And what did the Forest Master do to him?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_31c69c54:


    "The old man tilted his head and burst out laughing."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_166962b1:



    voice "voice/Hariton/51.S.ogg"
    Ded "It's easier to name what he didn't do ."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_b82f0110:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/63 An.ogg"
    Pol "Anton!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_5f4634f7:


    "The old man's eyes pinned me to the door leaf."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_8ea76d0d:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/64 A.ogg"
    Pol "Come on in, Anton!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_ed2e6a8b:


    "The old man stayed silent for a moment."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_bc798f8b:


    "Then he smiled as if nothing ever happened and rolled his wheelchair back."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_9621eea7:



    voice "voice/Hariton/52. N.ogg"
    Ded "My, look at me, talking your ear off. Go."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_6693f96e:


    "I brushed off my stupor and minced across the corridor."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_1dcfecf7:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/119. Pr.ogg"
    Ant "It was nice meeting you."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup_743f3460:



    voice "voice/Hariton/53.E.ogg"
    Ded "You too, Anton Petrov, you too..."


translate english mold_test_52ef9ebd:


    "I felt relieved when I finally slipped into Polina's room."


translate english mold_test_6760dbf0:


    "It looked just like its owner: cute and tidy."


translate english mold_test_b8342ba5:


    "A huge collection of vinyl records and a record player immediately caught my attention. The walls were adorned by framed photographs."


translate english mold_test_2132c864:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/65 De.ogg"
    Pol "I hope grandpa wasn't annoying you?"


translate english mold_test_a3b1b66c:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/120. Net.ogg"
    Ant "No. He's a very... intriguing person."


translate english mold_test_b9f3e5ba:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/66 Ne.ogg"
    Pol "I bet you know everything about your name by now."


translate english mold_test_2493dc0f:


    "I forced out a laugh. My eyes slid across the photos."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_player_21cb39c2:


    "This is an old-fashioned record player."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_player_31e9a4b0:


    "A bit too old-fashioned, but I like it! Let's see what Polina has in her collection. Vynil records from \"Melodia\" and some much rarer ones from \"Jugoton\", a company in Yugoslavia."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_player_e701c2f6:


    "Rakhmaninov, Sviridov, Verdi's arias performed by Hibla Gerzmava. Only classics—no Toto Cutugno, no Demis Roussos."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_player_73e27561:


    "She even has some \"bone music\". Recordings made with an electro recorder over x-ray shots. The needle slides on the picture of someone's ribs and you hear David Oistrakh playing a violin."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_piano_7cba8de6:


    "This is a well-maintained \"Kuzbass\" piano."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_piano_d6b8731e:


    "A \"Kuzbass\" piano. Not a speck of dust on the cover! This is the place where she practices. Let's see what pieces she has in her music sheets."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_piano_d18ef9b7:


    "Handel's \"Capriccio Sol Minor\". Looks like the name of a pizza Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles would eat. Meanwhile, I won't even be able to play a Flea Waltz."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_poster_b1ba1448:


    "That's a Sailor Moon poster."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_poster_3d198f0c:


    "A Sailor Moon poster. This cartoon is for girls! \"Transformers\" are way better, and drawing them is much more interesting, especially when they transform, when they change shape."


translate english d4_polhouse_lookaround2_poster_6465883c:


    "Although, if Polina has the \"2х2\" channel on her TV, and she invites me to watch it together, I won't refuse. In the name of the Moon, I shall punish you!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_099cf71b:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/121. A.ogg"
    Ant "Are these your parents?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_469a401d:


    "Polina looked down."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_cffc2019:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/67 Da.ogg"
    Pol "Yeah."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_92d29db6:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/68 Oni.ogg"
    Pol "They died many years ago... I can barely remember them."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_0c365ee4:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/122. O.ogg"
    Ant "Oh!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_9a068c29:


    "I felt like a total idiot. I could've guessed Polina was an orphan."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_fcdf3727:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/123. Mne.ogg"
    Ant "I'm so sorry."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_6f1c8e5a:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/69 Sp.ogg"
    Pol "Thank you."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_a454ba8b:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/70 De.ogg"
    Pol "Grandpa raised me as his own daughter. I'm forever grateful to him."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_14a5cc93:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/124. Pr.ogg"
    Ant "I can imagine how tough it was."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_2f4d4988:


    "Polina flashed me a sad smile and brushed off a mischievous lock of hair off her face."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_f04faf16:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/71 Da.ogg"
    Pol "Let's stop talking about sad stuff."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_0baa9dde:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/72 Po.ogg"
    Pol "Meet Johanna, instead."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_d61bfd97:


    "I bent down to take a better look at the cat that was snuggled up beside the radiator."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_74fc11b4:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/125. Pr.ogg"
    Ant "Hi, Johanna."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_b83e12aa:


    "The cat hit her tail on the radiator's fins. Then hissed, showing her fangs."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_2e614c5b:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/73 Pro.ogg"
    Pol "I'm sorry, she's not exactly friendly."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_f2c79cd4:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/125.K.ogg"
    Ant "I'm used to this kind of reaction."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_2d92707c:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/126.Ch.ogg"
    Ant "What's with that name, Johanna?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_1a601426:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/74 Te.ogg"
    Pol "Still not tired of talking about names?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_3c160cce:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/75 D.ogg"
    Pol "Johanna is from {u}\"Helen and the Boys\"{/u}. Have you seen it?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_b5a30c93:


    "I snorted."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_0515aaef:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/128. Et.ogg"
    Ant "That's a show for girls!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_d0537f32:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/76 Oi.ogg"
    Pol "Oh, come on. I for one, watch the \"Transformers\", too."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_1c1075b5:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/129.Da .ogg"
    Ant "Really now? And who's your favorite?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_18ee82ee:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/77 T.ogg"
    Pol "Is this a test? Well, let's say it's Megatron."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_4c361ba3:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/130. A.ogg"
    Ant "A-ha! Didn't you say you dislike bad guys?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_64fe3156:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/78 Da.ogg"
    Pol "I do, but he alone was able to thaw my heart!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_4dae7dd2:


    "Polina grabbed at her chest in a comical manner."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_8f34aaf1:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/131. tiz.ogg" 
    Ant "Did you know that Optimus and Megatron were friends and they fought against Cybertron's supremacy together?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_42ec4af4:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/131.No .ogg"
    Ant "But after Optimus was chosen as the new leader, Megatron went to the dark side."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_24acca0c:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/80 Bo.ogg"
    Pol "I'm afraid something similar might happen to you and Pyatifanov."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_eb37d98c:


    "I raised my eyebrows in surprise."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_8508f00d:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/132. Nu.ogg"
    Ant "Well, nobody chose me as the leader."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_c7ea9254:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/81 Do.ogg"
    Pol "Well, let's say I did."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_1334e9f8:


    "My face had probably turned red again."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_e72c969c:


    "Polina sat down on the couch and fixed the bedspread."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_44f3ee71:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/02 Chem.ogg"
    Pol "So, what are we gonna do?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_bc0a0296:


    "Her pose and playful gaze hypnotized me."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_d9e903cd:


    "Dimmed lights helped create a special, exciting atmosphere inside the room."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_23a31fd0:


    "I felt a faint aroma of blackberry, but also something more elusive and captivating."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_9e9895da:


    "At that moment, my usual embarrassment suddenly morphed into some unexplainable vigor."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_fb3f7f12:


    "I wanted to show off and brag, to do everything in my power to keep Polina's gaze fixed on me for as long as possible."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_90a3ee96:


    "I imagined myself to be like Agent 007, ready to seduce another femme fatale with his stunning looks."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_48ddbd8c:


    "As if mimicking the hero of spy action movies, I crossed my hands on my chest and, with a mysterious smile on my face, decided to lean against the wall."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_e53e29f5:


    "I thought myself to be quite charming at that particular moment."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_27947ec8:


    "Yet a clanking sound stopped me from enjoying this graceful pose. I failed to notice an open piano and sat down right in the middle of its keys."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_71a1d0ce:


    "I had lost all of my charms after almost reaching the ceiling in one scared jump."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_970d234b:


    "Followed by the instrument's lid slamming shut with a bang."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_69a414c2:


    "At the same time, a frightened Johanna jumped off the chair."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_51cc3bff:


    "The cat rushed up the curtain, and then dashed across the wall to the safety of the wardrobe's top, ripping out thin slices of wallpaper along the way."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_ca9829ce:


    "Pieces of a torn-up Sailor Moon poster that, by pure chance, happened to be in the way of the scared animal, fell to my feet."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_736a014f:


    "Judging from the look on Polina's face, she really liked that poster."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_abcc4a4e:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/40 Pro.ogg"
    Ant "S-sorry. I... it was an accident."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_fa283724:


    "She closed her eyes, her lips twisted and forehead wrinkled."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_d8630597:


    "It seemed like Polina was about to scream or cry, but she just sighed and spoke in a calm voice."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_01d5be98:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/05Ne.ogg"
    Pol "It's okay."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_f1f2365c:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/06 Net.ogg"
    Pol "There's nothing that can't be fixed with electric tape."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_75a3cb8e:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/07 Nu.ogg"
    Pol "Well, duct tape, in our case."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_357bcd37:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/08Dav.ogg"
    Pol "Give me a hand here."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_66d15447:


    "The last piece fell in its place and it seemed like the room's harmony was restored along with the poster."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_5449d1a1:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/42 Eto.ogg"
    Ant "This is a character from Sailor Moon, right? Sailor Jupiter, I think?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d0291747:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/09 Da.ogg"
    Pol "No way! This is Sailor Saturn!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_abf7c889:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/10 EE.ogg"
    Pol "Her name is Hotaru and she is a warrior of destruction. Yet instead of destroying the world, she ended up saving it."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d8082bbb:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/11 Mne.ogg"
    Pol "I've always liked her the most!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_b5ebdf04:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/12 Vot.ogg"
    Pol "So yeah... Oh, and she also has two different personalities in her, can you imagine?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_4c8b2a97:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/13 Po.ogg"
    Pol "She had, at the very least. Johanna ripped her into at least a dozen more!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_3bf1308d:


    "I glanced at Polina and inquired in a soft voice."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_c7771044:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/133. Ra.ogg"
    Ant "How do you usually spend your evenings?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_14a1dd5f:


    "Polina shrugged and looked at me as if bored."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_088813c9:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/83 Sm.ogg"
    Pol "I watch TV or play violin for Grandpa."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_530eb663:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/84 On.ogg"
    Pol "He wants to make me into a new {u}David Oistrakh{/u}."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_b998c81c:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/134. Ko.ogg"
    Ant "David who?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_be98040d:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/85 Sk.ogg"
    Pol "He was a famous violinist."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_1c83b9be:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/135. Ati.ogg"
    Ant "So he's forcing you to play?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_6ae7ffd5:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/86 Po.ogg"
    Pol "Forcing me? Nothing of the sort."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_3c096a75:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/87 Eto.ogg"
    Pol "This is my chance to move to a big city and lead a better life."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_228288e8:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/88 Ga.ogg"
    Pol "Touring different countries, meeting new people."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_586cb9ca:


    "I felt a sting of stupid jealousy from her words."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d718df22:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/136. Po.ogg"
    Ant "Can you play something for me?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_a4340c00:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/89 Ti.ogg"
    Pol "Are you sure?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_f8ee852c:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/137. Oche.ogg"
    Ant "Of course!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_ce5011b2:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/90 Hor.ogg"
    Pol "Alright... But keep in mind that I'm a bit under the weather today."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_9eb47e57:


    "She procured the violin from its case. The polished frame glimmered in the lamplight."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_dc9eaa41:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/91 Et.ogg"
    Pol "This is not an ordinary violin."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_8a5115ac:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/92 Ee.ogg"
    Pol "It was made in the seventeenth century by a violin artisan named Guarneri, and Oistrakh himself used it for his first concert."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_5907c3c2:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/138. Ona.ogg"
    Ant "Is it expensive?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_c8ea64d3:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/93 Nu.ogg"
    Pol "It's worth at least a couple million dollars."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_691361d8:


    "My jaw dropped. Polina replied with laughter."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d207d23b:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/94 Vi.ogg"
    Pol "I wish you could see your face right now!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_51198c38:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/95 Ya.ogg"
    Pol "I'm joking! It's dirt cheap."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d4b1420e:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/96 E.ogg"
    Pol "If I had one of Guarneri's violins, I would've lived in Moscow."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_5c98f4c9:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/139. A.ogg"
    Ant "Hey, I knew you were joking!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_781bd6d1:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/97 Ko.ogg"
    Pol "Mhm, suuure."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_09c6b58a:


    "Polina took a proper playing pose and clutched the violin between her shoulder and jaw. Then brought the bow to the strings."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_1e586011:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/98 Fa.ogg"
    Pol "Fa diez minor."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_0c2d3cd0:


    "The bow slid across the strings, saturating the air inside the room with music."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_7961d7fd:


    "I sat on the windowsill, amazed at the melody's power."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_39ace428:


    "Polina looked so graceful while playing!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_30a51d99:


    "Her bow soared, it cut open space-time."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_b3549926:


    "Her slender fingers moved with inhuman speed. A phantom smile smoldered on the girl's lips."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_625dec05:


    "It felt like the music, that mysterious fa diez minor, was akin to a gust of wind that found its way inside the house, bringing along smells of the sea and far-away cities."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_8687d58f:


    "And every new gust made it even more difficult to breathe for my enthralled self."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_0e5c8270:


    "The melody carried me up to the skies, bringing back memories of that night when I was jumping over the forest."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_26e91b75:


    "But just like everything good, it ended way too fast."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_ee0facbe:


    "Polina froze for a moment, then lowered her hand and bowed. The waterfall of her fragrant hair swayed back and forth."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_cec4d6af:


    "I jumped up, clapping."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_e73369fd:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/140. Br.ogg"
    Ant "Bravo! Who composed this?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_fbfaf639:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/100 Rob.ogg"
    Pol "Robert Schumann."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_67ea9b26:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/141. Vot.ogg"
    Pol "I have a new favorite composer now! Bra-"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_8322de20:


    "The second syllable turned into an incredulous cry when someone wailed under my foot."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_f20c5af0:


    "Johanna!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_6cd269aa:


    "I forgot all about the cat in all my excitement and ended up stepping on her tail."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_919a4fcf:


    "She didn't give me the time to apologize."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_7e361cc9:


    "Johanna crawled up my leg and clung to my thigh. Her sharp claws pierced my skin through the pants."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_f7d47d9a:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/142. Ai.ogg"
    Ant "Ow, ow, ow!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_c99f2533:


    "Polina came to my rescue by slapping the cat on the back of her head."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_ea3113bc:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/101 D.ogg"
    Pol "Johanna, you foul thing, shoo!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_f9fb7489:


    "The cat jumped on the wall rug and retreated from the room after opening the door with her paw."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_2ab3ddb3:


    "I winced when touching my thigh. It was probably quite scratched up."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_da37089e:


    "Polina gave me a sympathetic hug."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_5ad5bb3e:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/Bolno.ogg"
    Pol "Does it hurt?"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_9399d2b3:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/143. Da.ogg"
    Ant "Not really... It was my fault."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d04eea9c:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/102 Ya.ogg"
    Pol "I'll show her what attacking my guests entails!"


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_f1e9bf87:


    "I was worried less about the pain and more about the damage done to my clothes. My pants were riddled with tiny holes."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_ee7420ee:


    "Welp, Mom sure will be \"happy\" about this."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_e217f887:


    "At the same time, Polina's attention was flattering."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_bc2d0299:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/144.Tv .ogg"
    Ant "Your Johanna is quite a strong lady."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_e1f6465e:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/103 Vi.ogg"
    Pol "You'll get along."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_14b68f1c:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/104 Es.ogg"
    Pol "If you don't bleed out on me, of course."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_2651960c:


    "She turned around and searched the room with her eyes."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_d6acc62a:



    voice "voice/Polina/4day/105 Gd.ogg"
    Pol "I thought we had iodine around here."


translate english d4_polhouse_followup2_solved_7c108de9:



    voice "voice/anton/4day/145. Ne.ogg"
    Ant "Oh, don't worry..."


